{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1690"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c141): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c141.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1690"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge earth-space/astronomy","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/earth-space__astronomy.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",50],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",1],["-","everyday "],["=",828],["+","The astrolabe is a tool rather than a sight, but its name is just as literal: the „astrolabos“, the star-taker. This flat model of the heavens – a disc with a rotating star map and a sighting rule – was created by Greek astronomers more than a thousand years ago, with Hipparchus often credited, to determine the positions of the Sun and stars, tell the time and find one's latitude; perfected by astronomers of the Islamic world, it remained in use until the early modern era.\n\n"],["=",266],["+","Astrolabe | astrolabos | star-taker |\n| "],["=",11]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",50],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",1],["-","alltägliche "],["=",798],["+","Das Astrolabium ist eher ein Werkzeug als eine Himmelserscheinung, doch sein Name ist ebenso wörtlich: der „astrolabos“, der Sternnehmer. Dieses flache Modell des Himmels – eine Scheibe mit drehbarer Sternkarte und einem Visierlineal – wurde vor über tausend Jahren von griechischen Astronomen geschaffen, wobei man oft Hipparch als Urheber nennt, um die Positionen von Sonne und Sternen zu bestimmen, die Uhrzeit abzulesen und die geographische Breite zu finden; von Astronomen der islamischen Welt vervollkommnet, blieb es bis in die frühe Neuzeit in Gebrauch.\n\n"],["=",252],["+","Astrolabium | astrolabos | Sternnehmer |\n| "],["=",11]]}]},
